        "commit": {
          "id": "132ec2fe8160e410f38f14a0052dc12403c56de5",
          "message": "fix(store): never prune a just-created service's App on a stale snapshot (w8/m52)\n\nReconcileOnce reads desired rows before listing App CRs. A service whose row\nand complete App were both written between those two reads looked like an\norphan: the prune deleted its App, and the next pass recreated it from the row\nalone, dropping its pre-deploy command, health check and env-secret reference.\nProduction saw this as a service whose createdAt moved 13s after create and\nwhose accepted settings vanished while its URL returned 503.\n\nThe prune now re-reads the row with Store.GetApp and deletes only on a\ndefinitive ErrNotFound; any other read error keeps the App and reports a\nretryable error. The delete carries a UID precondition so a same-named\nreplacement is never removed by stale state. True orphans still converge.\n\nTests: the finding's probe (new App keeps UID and settings across two passes),\nan inconclusive row read, and a stale-UID replacement — all three fail on the\nold code. Files w8/071 for the namespace prune's matching shape."
        },
