          "message": "fix(blueprints): accept numeric env values the Render schema allows (w8/m53)\n\nThe pinned render.yaml schema types envVars[].value as string|number and the\ncompiler keeps a numeric scalar as int64/float64, but the typed adapter\nunmarshalled it into a string field, so `value: 47` failed validate, preview,\ncreate, sync and direct deploy with \"json: cannot unmarshal number into Go\nstruct field bexEnvVar...value of type string\" — in Bex and the unmodified\nRender CLI alike, at root, ungrouped, project-environment and env-group\nlocations.\n\nbexEnvVar now decodes value as raw JSON: a number keeps its JSON text (47,\n47.5, 1e3 -> 1000, 9007199254740993 exact — no float64 round trip); strings,\nomission and null decode as before. No schema, compiler or other field change."
        },
